---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import HeroArt from '../components/HeroArt.astro';import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
---
<Layout><section class="wrap hero"><div><span class="pill">✦ A playground for curious minds</span><h1>Learn to code.<br/>Make a little<br/><em>awesome.</em></h1><p>Big ideas, tiny steps. Turn “what if?” into games, art, and real Python programs. Your next adventure starts with a little curiosity.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button dark" href="/adventures/">Let’s start playing <span>→</span></a><a class="button ghost" href="/explore/">Find my adventure</a></div><div class="hero-proof"><span>Free to explore</span><span>No sign-up</span><span>Go at your pace</span></div></div><HeroArt/></section><div class="marquee"><span>Dream it.</span><b>✦</b><span>Try it.</span><b>✦</b><span>Oops? Tweak it.</span><b>✦</b><span>You made it!</span><b>✦</b><span>Do it all again.</span></div>
<section class="wrap" style="padding-top:42px"><div class="cta-band" style="background:var(--mint)"><div><span class="eyebrow">NEW · A whole world of coding ideas</span><h2>Meet your programming<br/>building blocks.</h2><p>Variables, if/else, loops, lists, and more. Learn by snapping real programs together in 20 playful missions.</p></div><a class="button dark" href="/blocks/">Explore the block trail →</a></div></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">A little curiosity goes a long way</span><h2>Fun coding activities<br/>for kids, from the first click.</h2></div><p>Start with a robot. Make your own art. Type your first line of Python. There’s more than one way to become a maker.</p></div><div class="grid3"><a class="card card-link tint-green" href="/adventures/"><div class="card-icon">↗</div><h3>Give Bit a mission</h3><p>Tell a little robot where to go. Collect stars and discover the magic of instructions and loops.</p><div class="topic-list"><span>New to coding</span><span>8 missions</span></div><div class="card-footer">Code adventures <span>↗</span></div></a><a class="card card-link tint-peach" href="/studio/"><div class="card-icon" style="background:#ffbb93">▦</div><h3>Think in pixels</h3><p>A tiny square can be the start of something big. Build colorful pixel art, one coordinate at a time.</p><div class="topic-list"><span>Creative explorers</span><span>Make & download</span></div><div class="card-footer">Pixel studio <span>↗</span></div></a><a class="card card-link tint-yellow" href="/python/"><div class="card-icon" style="background:#ffcf58">&gt;_</div><h3>Meet real Python</h3><p>Make your code talk, think, and repeat. Learn by changing real programs and seeing what happens.</p><div class="topic-list"><span>Ready to type</span><span>10 lessons</span></div><div class="card-footer">Python trail <span>↗</span></div></a></div></section>
<section class="section-soft"><div class="wrap section demo-band"><div class="demo-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Your first “I did that!”</span><h2>A little code.<br/>A big hello.</h2><p>Computers need instructions. This one says: “show my message.” Choose a message and see what happens when you run it.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div><h3>Pick an idea</h3><p>Every great thing starts with a little “what if?”</p></div></div><div class="step"><div><h3>Try. Tinker. Try again.</h3><p>Mistakes are clues. Follow them somewhere fun.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="demo-panel"><span class="pill">A tiny taste of Python</span><label for="hello-message">What should Bit say?</label><select id="hello-message"><option>I made this!</option><option>Hello, little universe!</option><option>Beep boop. Let's build!</option></select><pre><code id="hello-code">print("I made this!")</code></pre><button class="button dark" id="hello-run">▶ Run my message</button><div class="demo-result" id="hello-output" aria-live="polite">Your message lands here. ✨</div><p class="tiny">A preview of what <code>print()</code> does. Ready for real code? <a href="/python/hello-world/">Try lesson one →</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Made by you, obviously</span><h2>Don’t just play.<br/>Make the thing.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See all projects ↗</a></div><div class="grid3"><a class="card card-link" href="/playground/?project=story"><span class="pill peach">WORDS + A LITTLE WEIRD</span><h3>A silly story machine</h3><p>An otter. The Moon. Too many pancakes. Your code gets to tell the story.</p><div class="card-footer">Python project <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card card-link" href="/debug-detective/"><span class="pill">PUT YOUR THINKING HAT ON</span><h3>Become a bug detective</h3><p>Spot the tiny mistakes. Predict what happens. Collect a few “aha!” moments.</p><div class="card-footer">8 playful puzzles <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card card-link" href="/playground/?project=pet"><span class="pill yellow">YOUR NEW LITTLE SIDEKICK</span><h3>Build a pocket robot</h3><p>Give it a name, some energy, and a personality. Then teach it a new trick.</p><div class="card-footer">Python project <span>→</span></div></a></div></section>
<section class="wrap"><div class="cta-band"><div><span class="eyebrow">No perfect code required</span><h2>You bring the imagination.<br/>We’ll bring the starting line.</h2></div><a class="button dark" href="/explore/">Find your next thing →</a></div></section>
<section class="wrap section"><Faq items={[["Do I need to know anything about coding?","Nope! Start with Code Adventures. You can tap commands to guide Bit, with no typing needed. When you’re ready, the Python trail starts at the very beginning."],["What ages is Kids Code for?","The visual activities are designed with roughly ages 7–10 in mind. The Python trail suits confident readers and typists, often ages 10 and up. These are starting points, not rules: pick what feels interesting and ask a grown-up for a hand."],["Can I really run Python here?","Yes. The Python playground runs real Python in your browser. Nothing to install. The first run downloads the Python engine, so it needs an internet connection and may take a moment."],["Will my discoveries be saved?","Completed activities and your playground draft can be saved in this browser on this device. No account is needed. Clearing browser data removes that progress, and it does not sync to other devices."]]}/></section>
<script>const select=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#hello-message')!;const code=document.querySelector('#hello-code')!;select.addEventListener('change',()=>code.textContent='print('+JSON.stringify(select.value)+')');document.querySelector('#hello-run')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelector('#hello-output')!.textContent=select.value;});</script>
</Layout>
